      "kind": "content",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "The button stops counting at full",
      "detail": "At two and three the button names a number; at four it reads 'Delete all chats'. The user therefore loses the count at the point the action is most destructive, and the confirmation they land on is a different one from the counted path.",
      "nodes": [
        "8156:72875"
      ],
      "ask": "Should full selection read 'Delete 4 chats' and keep one confirmation, or is the all-chats wording deliberate?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "geometry",
      "severity": "low",
      "title": "The nav group collapses to one button",
      "detail": "The action group shrinks from 267px at x=102 to 123px at x=246 so that Cancel stays flush right. Nothing is drawn for the transition, so Cancel appears to jump.",
      "nodes": [
        "8156:72873"
      ],
      "ask": "Confirm Cancel holds its position while Select all leaves."
    }
